The old code called `cbor_get_uint16` directly without any type check. If `pairs[i].value` was not a uint at all (e.g., a string), `cbor_get_uint16` would read 2 bytes from the string's data pointer, which could be anywhere in memory. This is the original heap-buffer-overflow READ 2.

